# R2-INTERLUDE ruling 2, R2-HOME-TIERS (ledger D-86): the crossing review's home pictures. Sixteen
# home-time tiers (sim/home_tiers.ail, protocol 2.12), each a pool of variants tier<n>_v<k>.webp; the
# voyage's seed picks one per tier (time.variant; sim/data/home_variants.ail holds the counts, and
# `make home-art-check` checks this file, those counts and the files agree). Read by
# ui/crossing_review.gd (home_path; raw WebP, CaptainAvatar.make_texture) and shown as a 3:2 cover
# over the whole review panel on the Home page. Below 2.12 the host shows v0 of the old tier's place.
# Generated by Codex imagegen (driver codex exec -m gpt-6.1-sol; image model id not exposed), one
# style reference (assets/characters/medic/portrait_medic_y0_neutral.png, style only): the seven
# v0 pictures of tiers 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 13 on 2026-10-16 (approved by Mark that day; they were
# tier0..tier6), the v1 pictures of tiers 4, 6 and 8 from that session's other candidates, and every
# picture of tiers 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 12, 14 and 15 on 2026-10-19 (Mark, attended: every good
# candidate ships, D-86). Each keeps its left third calm for the text column. Every picture was
# inspected at 1:1 for text-like marks. Full provenance, every prompt verbatim and the excluded
# candidates: generation_notes.md (here).
#
# D-18 (big assets stay out of git): the masters are 1536x1024 RGB PNGs, kept in the public bucket at
# gs://stapledons-voyage-assets/site/<master sha256>.png (tools/site_media.sh asset; the website's
# concept-art page, website/src/data/concept.js HOME_FULL, shows tiers 0-12 only). The game ships lossy
# WebP at native 1536x1024, made with:
#   cwebp -q 88 -m 6 -sharp_yuv -metadata none <master>.png -o tier<n>_v<k>.webp   (libwebp 1.6.0)
# about 16 MB for the 28; each compared with its master at 1:1 (skies included): no visible banding.
# Format: tier<n>_v<k>.webp sha256 <webp> <- master sha256 <png> <url>
